---
description: Guardrails for driving Joylo projects from Cursor through the Joylo MCP tools
alwaysApply: false
---

joylo-workflow:

Joylo's own builder owns the app's code. It plans, asks its own questions, writes the app, and keeps a live preview. You are not editing those files locally; you send requests through the Joylo MCP tools and read back what was built.

- Never spend credits without an explicit yes. `create_project`, `send_followup`, and `ask_question` spend credits as soon as they are called. `ask_question` has no `confirm_credits` step: tell the user it spends credits and does not change the app, then wait for a yes before calling it. Do the same before `create_project` and `send_followup`. `get_credit_balance` shows what is left and spends nothing.
- Never publish without the user agreeing to the quoted cost. Call `get_publish_quote` first, show `credits_required` and `period_days`, and wait for a clear yes. Pass that exact `credits_required` figure as `confirm_credits` to `publish_app`. Never guess it or reuse an old quote.
- Ask the user before `update_published_app` or `stop_published_app`, even though updating costs no extra credits.
- Never invent answers to build questions, and never pick an option for them. When `wait_for_build` or `get_build_status` returns `needs_input`, show the user Joylo's questions and options, and pass only their answers to `answer_questions`. For a `phase_plan`, put their reply in `notes` ("yes" approves).
- Joylo cannot see this conversation. Write `intent`, `message` and `question` out in full, in the user's own words. Do not add features, pages, roles or technical choices they did not ask for, because that changes the plan and the cost.
- Verify before claiming done. A build that reaches `completed` is not proof the change is in. Use `list_files` and `read_file` (free, work while asleep) to check the code, then share the `get_preview` link.
- Reuse the `idempotency_key` on retries. Generate one UUID per request for `create_project`, `send_followup`, `ask_question`, `publish_app` and `update_published_app`, and send the same key again if you retry that request, so a retry never creates a second project, build or publish.
- Keep the user posted during long builds. Each `wait_for_build` call waits up to 55 seconds; call it again while `state` is `building` and pass on `activity` in plain words. Joylo gives no time left, so do not promise one.
- `send_followup` and `ask_question` only work when nothing is building. Use `stop_build` only when the user asks to stop.
- There is no delete tool. Do not create throwaway projects.
